# The id is <file>#<index> (the position in the file's list, from 0), with
# @<state> if the run starts in a state other than the data state.
#
# tools/conformance/html_tokenizer_suite.py fails the gate on a run that fails
# and is not listed here, AND on a listed run that no longer fails, so an entry
# cannot outlive its reason. None of these is a defect found and left: each is a
# vector that disagrees with the standard's text (retrieved 2026-10-11) and was
# read against it. The standard decides; the vectors are checked against it.
#
# Group 1: vectors that predate the processing instruction states (13.2.5.72 to
# 13.2.5.76). They were written when `<?` began a bogus comment with the error
# unexpected-question-mark-instead-of-tag-name, which is no longer in the list
# of parse errors. The comment they expect is the comment the tokenizer makes;
# only the error differs: it is raised as invalid-first-character-of-processing-
# instruction-target, one character later, by the state the standard now has.
